 ## Background
-This method originates from the Exolands project, an unofficial voxel engine implementation. It was designed to handle dynamic terrain updates efficiently by combining face culling with compact vertex storage.
+Originating from the Exolands project, this method was developed to handle dynamic voxel terrain in web-based games. It addresses the limitations of naive meshing by combining face culling with efficient vertex management. The approach is documented in the Exolands source code [S1, unofficial].
 
